  "title": "JSON: fix a displaying two-dimensional array bug in compact form",
  "description": "There is a bug to display JSON two-dimensional array in compact form. For example, to open a JSON file contains following content:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"storeName\": \"Book store\",\n  \"books\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"book1\",\n      \"pages\": 1020,\n      \"intArray\": [\n        1,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"endMember\": \"the last member of an object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"book2 \\\"quota\\\"\",\n      \"pages\": 623\n    }\n  ],\n  \"boolMember\": false,\n  \"subObject\": {\n    \"name\": \"jason\",\n    \"height\": 1.78\n  },\n  \"emptyObject\": {},\n  \"emptyArray\": [],\n  \"twoDimensionalArray\": [\n    [\n      1,\n      2,\n      3\n    ],\n    [\n      5,\n      6,\n      7\n    ]\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWireshark will display like:\n\n![wireshark_compact_form_bug](/uploads/d207f85997af310fd3e549ba55af0778/wireshark_compact_form_bug.jpg)\n\n\nThis MR will fix this bug. The correct parsing result should be:\n\n![wireshark_compact_form_bug_fixed](/uploads/c8192ffc503a8aaddfdf7c723f459fd5/wireshark_compact_form_bug_fixed.jpg)\n\nThis MR can be also cherry-picked to 3.6.x.",
